<title>UK: London tea auction sees strong demand.</title>
<headline>London tea auction sees strong demand.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Strong and active demand was seen at the latest Lndon tea auction, the Tea Brokers' Association of London said.</p>
<p>Among landeds, bright and coloury East Africans met keen competition and prices rose 5 to 10 pence. Plainer Central Africans were firm.</p>
<p>In the offshore sector, brighter liquoring Zimbabwes were strong and dearer but others were irregularly easier.</p>
</text>
